# CardScout always requests live prices. Practice numbers appear only when a
# configured live call fails. You do not set a demo mode here.
#
# On Vercel, set these so live mode stays on:
#   SCRYDEX_API_KEY
#   SCRYDEX_TEAM_ID
#   EBAY_CLIENT_ID
#   EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET
# PriceCharting is deferred. Leave PRICECHARTING_TOKEN blank until you subscribe.

# Raw English market prices from Scrydex (https://scrydex.com/), the successor
# to pokemontcg.io. CardScout does not call pokemontcg.io or dev.pokemontcg.io.
# A paid plan is required. Unauthenticated calls return 401.
# How to get the keys:
# 1. Register at https://scrydex.com/register
# 2. Subscribe at https://scrydex.com/pricing
#    Starter is $29/month and includes raw prices (5,000 credits).
#    Scrydex's FAQ says graded prices and history start on higher plans.
#    This app only reads the raw Near Mint USD market, so Starter covers it.
# 3. Create a team in the account hub and copy the team ID.
# 4. Generate an API key. CardScout sends X-Api-Key and X-Team-ID.
# Docs: https://scrydex.com/docs/getting-started/authentication
# Prices: https://scrydex.com/docs/getting-started/prices
# The market field is a USD average across US sources, not a TCGPlayer-only
# number. Variants can include a TCGPlayer purchase link.
# Leave these blank and the raw box says it is not configured. No prices are invented.
SCRYDEX_API_KEY=
SCRYDEX_TEAM_ID=

# eBay sold comps. Client credentials from https://developer.ebay.com/.
# How to get them:
# 1. Create an application and a keyset.
# 2. Copy the Client ID and Client Secret.
# 3. Ask eBay to allow Marketplace Insights for that app.
# Browse item_summary/search only returns active listings. It has no sold or
# completed filter, so CardScout does not use Buy It Now asks as sold prices.
# Sold search calls /buy/marketplace_insights/v1_beta/item_sales/search
# with scope https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/buy.marketplace.insights
# Leave the keys blank and the eBay box says Not configured. No sold prices are invented.
EBAY_CLIENT_ID=
EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET=
# PRODUCTION or SANDBOX. Defaults to PRODUCTION.
EBAY_ENV=PRODUCTION

# Deferred. Graded slab prices. The Values slot stays, and this wiring stays.
# Until this is set, that box says "Coming soon" and "Not configured".
# No graded prices are invented.
# How to get it later:
# 1. Subscribe at https://www.pricecharting.com/
# 2. Open the subscription page → API/Download.
# 3. Copy the token. CardScout sends it as the `t` query parameter.
# Docs: https://www.pricecharting.com/api-documentation
# The API returns current grades only. It does not return the history chart.
PRICECHARTING_TOKEN=
